   "scope": "life"
  },
  {
   "id": "ex:episode-7f1aaf4a95ce752b363c4abf3b",
   "kind": "episode",
   "label": "person:admin: How do you keep it in good shape at the end of the day? Lumen: At the end of…",
   "text": "person:admin: How do you keep it in good shape at the end of the day? Lumen: At the end of the day, I help people keep their tools in good shape through a few simple practices: **1. Cleaning** - Wipe down each tool with a clean cloth to remove wood dust - Pay special attention to crevices where debris can hide - A damp cloth works well for most tools **2. Drying** - Ensure tools are completely dry before storage - Wood handles should never stay damp - this can cause cracking **3. Do you have a particular ritual for tool care?",
